1
00:00:07,110 --> 00:00:10,460
A cyclist starts at a speed of U metres per second.

2
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:13,790
She speeds up by A metres per second every second.

3
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:17,670
After T seconds, her speed is V equals U plus A T.

4
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:23,280
Her final speed is 14, her starting speed is 2, and T is 4 seconds.

5
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:24,990
Find A, her acceleration.

6
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:28,570
Pause the video and work it out.

7
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:30,350
14 equals 2 plus 4 A.

8
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,620
Take away 2: 12 equals 4 A.

9
00:00:32,670 --> 00:00:37,900
Divide by 4: A equals 3 metres per second, every second.

10
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:43,930
Remember: to solve an equation, do the same to both sides, to undo each operation.

11
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:46,630
A formula is a rule that links variables.

12
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:49,200
The variable on its own is the subject.

13
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:52,450
In V equals U plus A T, the subject is V.

14
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:58,150
Changing the subject means rearranging, so that a different variable is on its own.

15
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:01,800
Subtract U from both sides, then divide by T.

16
00:01:01,850 --> 00:01:02,450
Your turn.

17
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:05,230
Make T the subject of V equals U plus A T.

18
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:08,410
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:10,560
Subtract U: V minus U equals A T.

20
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:12,000
This time divide by A.

21
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:14,760
So T equals V minus U, all over A.

22
00:01:14,810 --> 00:01:17,130
You can write your own formula.

23
00:01:17,180 --> 00:01:22,390
A plumber charges a 40 dollar call-out fee, plus 25 dollars per hour.

24
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:26,600
The cost C for H hours is C equals 40 plus 25 H.

25
00:01:26,650 --> 00:01:31,930
Rearrange it to find the hours: H equals C minus 40, over 25.

26
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:33,300
Here is the method.

27
00:01:33,350 --> 00:01:36,090
Step 1: circle the new subject.

28
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:40,000
Step 2: undo the operations around it, in reverse order.

29
00:01:40,050 --> 00:01:42,370
Do the same to both sides.

30
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:46,070
Step 3: keep fractions and brackets clear.

31
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:49,550
Step 4: check by substituting numbers.

32
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:52,440
Make H the subject of A equals a half B H.

33
00:01:52,490 --> 00:01:55,270
Multiply both sides by 2: 2 A equals B H.

34
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:58,440
Then divide by B: H equals 2 A over B.

35
00:01:58,490 --> 00:01:59,120
Your turn.

36
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:01,800
Make B the subject of the same formula.

37
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:04,710
Pause and work it out.

38
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:05,790
2 A equals B H.

39
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,370
This time divide by H.

40
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:09,580
So B equals 2 A over H.

41
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:12,530
Make R the subject of A equals pi R squared.

42
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:15,280
Divide by pi: R squared equals A over pi.

43
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:17,580
Then take the square root.

44
00:02:17,630 --> 00:02:20,700
Max makes A the subject of V equals U plus A T.

45
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:22,570
Which line is wrong?

46
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:23,670
Line 1 is wrong.

47
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:26,480
Adding U was done last, so undo it first.

48
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:29,020
Subtract U, then divide by T.

49
00:02:29,070 --> 00:02:30,380
V minus U equals A T.

50
00:02:30,430 --> 00:02:32,870
So A equals V minus U, over T.

51
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:36,590
Doctors rearrange formulae to work out medicine doses.

52
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:42,870
Engineers rearrange V equals U plus A T to design brakes that stop a train in time.

53
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:44,110
One last question.

54
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:46,880
Make X the subject of Y equals X over 4.

55
00:02:46,930 --> 00:02:50,150
Pause the video and answer.

56
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:53,760
X was divided by 4, so multiply both sides by 4.

57
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:55,290
X equals 4 Y.

58
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:59,440
To remember: the subject is the variable on its own.

59
00:02:59,490 --> 00:03:02,770
Use inverse operations, in reverse order.

60
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:05,610
A square is undone by a square root.

61
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:07,920
Check with numbers.

62
00:03:07,970 --> 00:03:13,150
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.6 on Camday.
